      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/734679</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/734679#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">9600238e6a19e9de9b246f3ff0b6ffbdd9290f23</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:04:58 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae850eb4cdf7.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bc3775.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0ba1986.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0b80f7c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bb9b53.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bd88f5.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bce35c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0ae9503.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Ultimate Ascend&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Warning:&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;A user has suggested that the latest version of this mod doesn't work. If the same applies to you, please use the older "descend" build (only works on 1.2.1) until I get this sorted.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Descend is now Ultimate Ascend! Ascend through all sky islands, &lt;b&gt;ascend through the depths ceiling&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;descend&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; through the surface to the depths or descend through sky islands, physics objects, sky islands, etc. If you can ascend to it you can likely descend backward to it as well.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Activate Ascend normally for infinite ascend, click L3 and you'll see the "Descend" prompt instead of "Ascend". You can now descend to ceilings beneath you rather than merely ascend through ceilings above you. When on the surface of Hyrule, if there isn't a cavity such as a cave, construction, etc. beneath you - you will see the "Depths" instead of "Descend". This means you can descend into the depths at that spot!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The descend marker will (try to) help you by changing from red to green based on how close you are to "descend-able" ground. It doesn't work terribly well. The game just isn't designed around the concept of descending unlike ascend. But I still find it's better than having only an on/off detector.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The mod is an exefs-patch/ipchtxt, so it doesn't occupy a subsdk slot and can be used with other mods mostly conflict-free (unless they are dealing with similar concepts like another ascend mod).&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod is a successor to my Infinite Ascend mod, which is now legacy/deprecated. This has more features than that one.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Recent Changes&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;v0.16.0 adds support for every version of TotK&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;v0.16.0 renames the mod from Descend to Ultimate Ascend, combining features from my former Infinite Ascend mod with the new Descend feature and the ability to now ascend to any Sky Island.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;v0.15.1 fixes conflict with the excellent &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/723719"&gt;Ascend Through Depth Ceiling&lt;/a&gt; mod.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Installation&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Emulator: extract the &lt;b&gt;descend&lt;/b&gt; folder into the game's mod directory and enable Descend.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Atmosphere: copy the archive's &lt;b&gt;exefs_patches/descend&lt;/b&gt; folder into &lt;b&gt;atmosphere/exefs_patches/descend&lt;/b&gt; on the SD card.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Link's feet sometimes don't appear at the descend destination, particularly when the exit is sloped or jagged.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The camera can sometimes appear inside of a wall, revealing an "out of bounds" area when previewing an exit at your destination.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In rare instances, you may wind up inside of a wall/out-of-bounds area. Warping to a shrine is your only option here.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Animations/Swirling can look janky at times.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Limitations&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;b&gt;Only tested on Switch running v1.2.1 of the game. Highly unlikely to work on other versions.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;AI Disclaimer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This project was developed with heavy help from AI Codex Astra 6. For an overview of how I develop ExeFS mods using AI please see this post &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739"&gt;https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Donations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you enjoy my work, feel free to &lt;a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/hansoloblaster" target="_blank"&gt;buy me a coffee&lt;/a&gt;! I provide the mod and its source code completely free and open source. I stand by that; so only donate if you're feeling friendly or would like to boost my spirits!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/descend-v0150_-wz2v1I.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/descend-v0151-ascend-free-compat_-Dn2M0o.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/descend-v0151-switch.zip" type="application/zip"/>
