      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6adfc67a1c3fa.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6adfc7f46c63e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;This changes all the quick menus in the game to be fast again, similar to how fast they were in BotW. That includes changing &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Weapons, Bows, Shields and Materials&lt;/span&gt;, quick &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;dropping stuff&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;and &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;quick fusing stuff&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;to Arrows&lt;/span&gt; from the quick menu, and the &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Special Power&lt;/span&gt; wheel closes faster too.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;There’s &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;no more delay after letting go of the D-pad&lt;/span&gt;, and the menu also &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;opens a bit quicker&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src="https://files.gamebanana.com/bitpit/equip2.gif"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For some reason they added this big delay in TotK compared to BotW and it always bothered me, but it was just a simple fix.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It supports Version &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;1.1.0 - 1.4.3&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;TKMM isn’t necessary&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Have fun.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
