ebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac6fb1a89a25.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac6fb1ab0c46.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac6fb1ab1a1f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac6fb1ab2c49.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Actor Edit&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tweak&lt;/em&gt;: Edited the Daisy Golf Actor, The subfile had a typo to it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hello!&lt;br&gt;I'm happy to present a big armor pack mod for the playable Riju mod! &lt;br&gt;Behold, a big 8 armor set pack that consists of two different sports outfits that the 3 princesses worn in Mario Tennis Aces and Mario Golf Super Rush. Including two outfits that the diva herself Pauline worn in those games too as well.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Doing this whole thing took me weeks to finish and honestly, I'm really happy with how this turned out. This is my first mod that I have ever done that involves porting models from a different game into Tears, and learning blender was no small feat since that took a lot of will power to do and learn over time.&lt;br&gt;(Thanks a bunch for teaching/helping me Alpha)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each armor part's defense is 28 and putting on 3 gives 84 defense in total. I decided to not add any effects or make this op because the other 3 outfit mods I did are already op as it is. &lt;br&gt;Wearing them as a set gives an attack buff as well so I feel like that is fair enough.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All of these outfits can be bought from the Beedle shop in Kara Kara Bazar&lt;br&gt;(Some the armor parts will cost 4k rupees, since most of these were done over the wild set not hard to grind rupees honestly lol)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;What is even more amazing is that the 4 dresses have skirt physics, and 7 of the 8 outfits have working hair physics too! &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Anyways, enjoy the mod! I will be trying to make more standalone Riju outfits down the line. &lt;br&gt;I love the playable RIju mod so much lol, it's literally the best playable character mod I ever seen so far. The Mario styled font was made through a font generator, and the thumbnail picture was made though using GIMP&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;One mod I do suggest downloading is the invisible battery mod &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/453885"&gt;Invisible Batteries Mod for The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom | TOTK Mods&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;since the battery placement on some costumes isn't right and I couldn't really figure that out tbh.</description>
